WEBVTT

00:00:00.470 --> 00:00:02.132
As a former IELTS examiner,

00:00:02.132 --> 00:00:05.025
the overview is the first thing I look for in a

00:00:05.025 --> 00:00:07.610
Task 1 answer. So let's mark one together.

00:00:08.320 --> 00:00:10.120
Here's the commuting graph.

00:00:10.120 --> 00:00:13.253
It shows how long it took people to get to work

00:00:13.253 --> 00:00:15.920
in three cities. And here's an overview:

00:00:16.500 --> 00:00:20.744
“Overall, the commute in Oakhaven increased from

00:00:20.744 --> 00:00:24.811
20 to 45 minutes, in Tarnbridge from 25 to 32,

00:00:24.811 --> 00:00:27.640
and in Stellmoor from 30 to 35.”

00:00:28.150 --> 00:00:28.960
Get your pen ready.

00:00:29.540 --> 00:00:32.101
Every number in this sentence is correct.

00:00:32.101 --> 00:00:33.663
But it isn't an overview.

00:00:33.663 --> 00:00:35.100
It's a list of figures.

00:00:35.700 --> 00:00:38.871
So I'll circle each number and move it to where

00:00:38.871 --> 00:00:41.030
it belongs: the body paragraphs.

00:00:41.540 --> 00:00:44.796
Now cover the numbers on the graph and ask two

00:00:44.796 --> 00:00:47.840
questions. What is true of all three lines?

00:00:48.430 --> 00:00:49.210
They all went up.

00:00:49.980 --> 00:00:51.280
Which line is different?

00:00:51.670 --> 00:00:54.808
Oakhaven. It started with the shortest commute

00:00:54.808 --> 00:00:56.650
and ended with the longest.

00:00:57.480 --> 00:00:59.050
Put those two answers together:

00:00:59.810 --> 00:01:02.857
“Overall, commuting times rose in all three

00:01:02.857 --> 00:01:05.762
cities, and Oakhaven went from having the

00:01:05.762 --> 00:01:08.100
shortest commute to the longest.”

00:01:08.620 --> 00:01:11.407
No figures. Just one sentence that tells the

00:01:11.407 --> 00:01:13.180
reader what the graph shows.

00:01:13.750 --> 00:01:16.560
Now mark the overviews on the right page.
